    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) reaching 3+ members now yields `membershipTier = \"GOLD\"`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a read-time derived field. The mapper (`OwnerMapper`) computes SILVER/BRONZE purely from stored `Owner` fields but has no repository access to count household members. I followed the codebase's existing pattern for repository-dependent read-time enrichment (`bulkSignupWarning`, computed in the single-owner responders):\n\n- **New `HouseholdMembership` helper** (`rest/function/owner/HouseholdMembership.java`) \u2014 `isGold(owner, repo)` counts owners sharing the owner's `householdId` and returns true at 3+ members (guarding against null/blank household ids).\n- **`RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 after mapping, override `dto.setMembershipTier(\"GOLD\")` when `isGold` holds. These are the two responders that already inject `OwnerRepository`, matching how `bulkSignupWarning` is applied.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe flow works because `AssignHousehold` (run during create) stamps the shared `householdId` onto every household member, so by the time the third member is created all three share it, the count is 3, and both the create response and later GETs return GOLD.",
